- units AI 9 vs player 1 (16 legacy gap).
- tiles player 13 vs AI 11 (player +4 legacy).
- techs equal 2.
- gold AI 13/10=1 vs player 0 (1).
- AI monument bonus 4.
Total gap 37.

So the AI's main advantage is units (9) and buildings (4). If we cap AI army at 5 and slow production, gap shrinks: units 9->5 saves 8; buildings maybe AI still 4 vs player 2 (player could build more with less military spending). If player builds 2 more buildings, +8. Then scores closer.

But player only had 2 buildings because of constant military production. With a cap/slower AI, player can build more. Also player had 1 unit at end because AI killed them; with less AI pressure, player retains more units (legacy +2 each) and can build.

So balance changes:
1. Cinderhold starting prod 11 -> 5 (prevents free warrior; AI first warrior turn 3 or 4).
2. AI army cap 5, with production logic to build economy after 5. Actually if army cap 5 and player has 3-5, AI won't snowball to 9.
