Player 88 vs AI 114. Buildings 1 vs 4! Why did the player only build 1 building despite walls priority? Because production kept resetting to warrior when fighters<2. Fighters count dropped to 1 at turn 12, so it rebuilt warriors. Also walls may never complete because fighters<2 resets production each turn? Let's see: `setProduction` every turn sets warrior when fighters<2. At turn 9 fighters=2, walls before (turn<=7) false, so granary. But why only 1 building? Maybe the player was still building warriors/granary but production resets when fighters drop. The build order sets production every turn; if it changes from walls to warrior, progress carries over but the same production pool, so switching loses? Actually production carries over, but item changes; city.prod accumulates and completes current item. If it switches to warrior at 16 cost, it completes a warrior and then resets to ai? For player, production after completion defaults to warrior. So it may keep producing warriors.

At T4 fighters=2, T5 walls priority (turn<=7) -> set walls. T5-T7 walls. T8 fighters=2, wallsBefore false (turn 8), sets granary. Walls might not have completed (cost 30, prod ~5, 3 turns = 15, not enough) and is abandoned. Then granary, but at T12 fighters=1, resets warrior. So the player never completes walls. This is a strategy issue: switching projects loses time. A human would stick with walls. Our simulation switches every turn based on priority, and since wallsBefore flips at turn 8, it abandons walls halfway. Fix: don't switch away from walls until built. Similarly, don't switch away from a building to warrior unless city is in danger. A human would commit.

Let's write production logic that commits:
- If city.prodItem is a building under construction and not built, keep it unless the city is under immediate threat and has no garrison.
- Priorities: if no walls and turn<=9, set walls and keep. Else granary etc.

Also fighters<2 triggers warrior even when building. Need to only build warrior if no garrison / city HP low. A human would keep building walls even with 1 warrior, fortify, and heal. Let's adjust:
```
if (!has('walls') && state.turn <= 10) item='walls';
else if (fightersCount<2 && !cityUnderThreat) item='warrior'; ...
```
But if we keep walls and the lone warrior dies, city is vulnerable. Yet walls give city HP/defence. It might be okay.

Let's adjust simulation to commit to walls first, then economy. Build warrior only if fighters==0 and no walls? Hmm.

Actually the player starts with 1 warrior and 1 scout. The scout can fight (strength 4) but we didn't count it. We only count warrior/spearman. The AI attacks the warrior; when it dies, the scout could defend. But weak.

Let's count scout as a defender? It canFight. But we keep it collecting features. After features collected, it could garrison. Maybe.

The bigger issue: the AI's 4 buildings give 16+4=20 legacy, while player has 1. To win, player must build. The AI has enough production to do both units and buildings; player can't because it's spending on units to replace losses.

Maybe the game is inherently asymmetric and hard. We can adjust the AI to be less of a builder: reduce its building priority or make it spend more on units (which are capped) so it wastes production. If AI caps at 4 units and has 4 buildings, it's efficient. If we lower AI's production (starting 6, maybe 5), it will get fewer buildings. Also, AI's `aiChooseProduction` prioritizes granary, workshop, library, walls, market, monument. That's 6 buildings. It got 4 by turn 20 (granary, workshop, library, walls? plus monument bonus 4 means monument built too = 5? breakdown buildings 4 + legacyBonus 4 implies monument among 4). So AI built 4.

If we want the player to catch up, reduce AI production to 5 or cap AI buildings? Or boost player production. The player's Sunfall yields 4 prod vs AI 5. After improvements, player can get to 6-8. But the player has 13-16 tiles, more than AI, yet prod only 4? Wait cityYields works only the best `pop` tiles; pop 7, so 7 tiles. The player improved tiles? The worker improved 1 per turn; probably many. Player should have good prod. But in the breakdown, buildings 1. Let's inspect player city yields at end. It may have production but not enough time.

Let's get detailed turn-by-turn production? We can inspect at final. Maybe the player only has 1 building because production kept switching. Fix the sim and see.

Let's modify sim production:
```
const current = capital.prodItem;
const currentIsBuilding = !!BUILDINGS[current] && !has(current);
const underThreat = capital.hp < capital.maxHp || s.units.filter(ai within 3).length > 0;
if (currentIsBuilding) keep current;
else {
  if (!has('walls') && state.turn <= 12) walls;
  else if (!has('granary')) granary;
  else if (!has('workshop')) workshop;
  else if (!has('monument')) monument;
  else if (!has('library')) library;
  else if (!has('market')) market;
  else warrior;
}
```
No fighter replacement. Keep 1 warrior + scout. If warrior dies, maybe produce warrior only if no fighters at all and no walls? Let's allow if fighters==0 and not currentIsBuilding, produce warrior. But if walls under construction, keep walls.

Let's test. Also count scout as fighter for defense count? Not needed.

We also need to ensure the warrior stays fortified on city and heals. The sim sets it every turn; good.

Run.

